#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/creating_models/4-comparing-full-and-reduced-order-models.ipynb:9
msgid "Comparing full and reduced-order models"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/creating_models/4-comparing-full-and-reduced-order-models.ipynb:20
msgid ""
"In the `previous notebook <./3-negative-particle-problem.ipynb>`__ we saw "
"how to solve the problem of diffusion on a sphere, motivated by the problem "
"in the negative particle in battery modelling. In this notebook we consider "
"a reduced-order ODE model for the particle behaviour, suitable in the limit "
"of fast diffusion. We also show how to compare the results of the full and "
"reduced-order models."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/creating_models/4-comparing-full-and-reduced-order-models.ipynb:22
msgid ""
"In the limit of fast diffusion in the particles the concentration is uniform "
"in :math:`r`. This result in the following ODE model for the (uniform) "
"concentration in the particle"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/creating_models/4-comparing-full-and-reduced-order-models.ipynb:24
msgid "\\frac{\\textrm{d} c}{\\textrm{d} t} = -3\\frac{j}{RF}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/creating_models/4-comparing-full-and-reduced-order-models.ipynb:29
msgid "with the initial condition:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/creating_models/4-comparing-full-and-reduced-order-models.ipynb:31
msgid "\\left.c\\right\\vert_{t=0} = c_0,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/creating_models/4-comparing-full-and-reduced-order-models.ipynb:36
msgid ""
"where :math:`c` is the concentration, :math:`r` the radial coordinate, :math:"
"`t` time, :math:`R` the particle radius, :math:`D` the diffusion "
"coefficient, :math:`j` the interfacial current density, :math:`F` Faraday's "
"constant, and :math:`c_0` the initial concentration."
msgstr ""

